/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Collaborative, model-driven development. Mendix is built around a strongly model-driven approach in which visual domain models, microflows, and page designs are the actual application logic rather than a scaffold for generated code, and it places heavy emphasis on structured collaboration between professional developers and business stakeholders working in the same visual canvas simultaneously. This collaborative editing model is frequently cited as a differentiator from platforms where business and IT contributors work in separate tools. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Cloud-native and integration capabilities. The platform natively supports microservices, container-based deployment through Kubernetes, and multi-cloud hosting across Mendix Cloud, AWS, Azure, and private infrastructure, giving architecture teams flexibility in how and where applications run. Its data-modeling layer connects cleanly to SAP landscapes in particular, which combined with the Siemens relationship makes it a common choice for large manufacturing and industrial organizations already running SAP as a system of record. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Background and positioning. OutSystems was founded in Portugal in 2001 and has grown into one of the most recognized names in the enterprise low-code category, built specifically around the idea that large, mission-critical systems can be delivered visually without sacrificing the rigor professional development teams expect. Unlike SMB- oriented builders, OutSystems targets IT departments and systems integrators building applications that must scale to thousands of concurrent users, integrate with legacy back-end systems, and survive years of iterative enhancement. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Architecture and technical depth. The platform compiles visual models into standard technology stacks \(Java or .NET on the back end, Angular/React-based single-page applications on the front end\) rather than interpreting them at runtime, which gives OutSystems applications performance characteristics close to hand-coded software. Built-in support for microservices architecture, containerized deployment, and horizontal scaling makes it a realistic choice for applications that must handle enterprise-scale transaction volumes rather than departmental workloads. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (DevOps and governance tooling. A defining strength is OutSystems' full application lifecycle management: integrated version control, automated regression testing, one-click rollback, and a dedicated architecture dashboard that flags technical debt and detects cross-application dependencies before they cause outages. This lets platform teams apply the same governance discipline to low-code applications that they would apply to traditionally coded systems, which is a major reason large regulated enterprises favor it over lighter-weight tools. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Pricing and ideal buyer. OutSystems does not publish list pricing; enterprise contracts are individually negotiated based on the number of applications, end users, and environments, and typically represent a significant investment relative to SMB-focused platforms. It is best suited to enterprises with dedicated IT or platform engineering teams that need to build and maintain a portfolio of complex, long-lived applications, rather than business users looking to build a single departmental tool quickly. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
